     "answer": 1,
     "why": "Konjed is sesame and -daar means 'having'; saade is 'plain'.",
     "lesson": "Bread questions elsewhere are often about size, and saade can also mean 'simple', so 'small' tempts; the ending -daar ('with, having') is the clue."
